{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123232","id":4453336984,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCXCHmA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123232","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123232.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123232.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123232","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123232/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123232/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123232/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/776bf054c322d0e55529054fb44ad0d195dd7f61","number":123232,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Introduce dedicated lint pass for GDScript to isolate warnings","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nOur current approach to emitting warnings is doing it somewhere within the parser or analyzer and wrapping it in `ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED`. This approach piggybacks on the existing tree walking that those classes do, however I've personally grown a bit disillusioned with it. In particular I've noticed a certain pattern of conversation on RocketChat, were I end up saying \"yeah we could add a warning about that\" and then I think about whether I actually want to add code to the analyzer for it and am not so sure about it anymore.\r\n\r\nThis PR implements a new approach for emitting warnings: An additional pass over the AST that runs after the analyzer, in lack of a better term I named it `GDScriptLinter`. The lint pass works on a fully analyzed and immutable AST and can easily be omitted for e.g. autocompletion.\r\n\r\nI won't claim that this is better then what we currently have in all regards. So here are the things I've considered:\r\n\r\nCon:\r\n- Might be harder to access certain context (which is also why I have no intention of realizing all warnings through this. But a lot of warnings are straight forward when looking at a fully analyzed part of the AST.)\r\n- More boilerplate\r\n- Probably slower due to the additional tree walking (haven't done profiling though, and especially the re-analyzation of dependencies, might have a pretty unpredictable influence on the performance of this)\r\n\r\nPro:\r\n- Warnings can be implemented outside of the analyzer\r\n  - Makes reviewing and writing those warnings easier, since the tree is fully analyzed, which prevents \"oh you are accessing the type of A but A has not been analyzed at this point yet\" errors.\r\n  - Less `ifdef` in the analyzer -> see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121047 for why I think this is desireable\r\n- It's easy to omit checks for autocompletion, which is good for more expensive checks\r\n\r\nI personally think it's worth it based on those factors. Happy to hear contrary positions though.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI've chosen the `CONFUSABLE_IDENTIFER` warning to demonstrate the system. I think it's a great example because it is on the one hand probably the worst case in terms of boilerplate (identifiers are used frequently and applying something only to declarations requires filtering for node types above `IdentifierNode`, while a lot of other warnings can be pinned to more specific nodes) and on the other hand it is a pretty expensive warning so omitting it for autocompletion makes sense (see my probably slightly outdated flamegraph in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/80637#issuecomment-2213373887 for that).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repite